# Frontend runtime is same-origin first for /api and /ws.
# Leave these unset for the normal one-build-per-product deployment model.
# Only set VITE_API_BASE_URL when you intentionally run the frontend against a separate API origin.
# `localhost` is for internal health/backend checks only and must not be the official clinic URL.

# Optional split-origin override example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# The example above is a SAME-SITE split (frontend clinic.example.com + API
# api.example.com share the site): the csrf_token cookie's default
# SameSite=Lax is delivered on withCredentials POSTs. For a CROSS-SITE split
# (different registrable domains, e.g. a *.vercel.app frontend), also set
# CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE=none on the API (see backend.env.sample) — otherwise
# the browser withholds the cookie on cross-site POSTs and the backend
# rejects them with 403 missing_cookie.
